    description: "Repro (2026-10-06, hypergumbo dev + WI-bapal branch): repo exfx with a.py (def hi) and lib/b.py (def lo). XDG_CACHE_HOME=fresh; 'hypergumbo survey exfx'; 'hypergumbo survey exfx -e lib'; then 'hypergumbo search lo exfx' prints 'No symbols found matching lo' -- the user never asked a read command to exclude lib/. Both surveys write one results dir (sketch_embeddings._get_results_cache_dir keys on repo state + resolved backends + trace_deps token + analyzer identity; extra_excludes is not in it). Violated invariant: a cached artifact is reused only by runs with the same analysis configuration (cf. WI-givib for backends, WI-bapal for --trace-deps). Fix shape: suffix the state segment with a hash of the normalised extra excludes when non-empty, as trace_deps does; decide whether read commands should then find an excluded survey (likely not, as with one-off backend flags)."  # a0cc
    fields: {}  # a0cc
